// Organizations from the command line (SPEC 29): `symbolon device org ...`.
//
//   org new DIR NAME                 PIN; founds an organization; prints "ORG-ID FOUNDER"
//   org join DIR ORG-ID FOUNDER [CODE]   PIN; this device's organization; CODE answers an invite
//   org invite DIR EXT-ID NAME [GROUP,...]   PIN; an invite for one person; prints "CODE ID"
//   org show DIR                     "org ID NAME-HEX", "version V gov G", "role R", policy, recovery
//   org members DIR                  "LOG NAME-HEX EXT-HEX|- owner|admin|member GROUP-IDS|-"
//   org add DIR LOG NAME [EXT-ID]    PIN; an owner or administrator adds a person
//   org remove DIR LOG               PIN; takes them out of the organization and every group
//   org role DIR LOG owner|admin|member   PIN; an owner changes someone's role
//   org policy DIR KEY VALUE         PIN; an owner changes the policy
//   org group new DIR NAME           PIN; prints the group's id
//   org group add|remove DIR GROUP LOG    PIN
//   org groups DIR                   "GROUP-ID NAME-HEX PEOPLE"
//   org folder new DIR NAME GROUP[,GROUP...]   PIN; a group folder; prints its id
//   org sync DIR                     PIN; an owner or administrator adds those who answered invites,
//                                    then re-keys the group folders people left
//   org recovery on DIR K DELAY ADMIN-LOG,... [--short-delay]   PIN; an owner turns on opt-in recovery (SPEC 29.8)
//   org recovery off DIR             PIN
//   org escrow DIR CID               PIN; a work folder you own, escrowed to the recovery key
//   org recover request|approve|open DIR CID   PIN; recovery administrators open a work folder
//   org export DIR [--https URL [--token T]] [--syslog HOST:PORT] [--ca FILE]   verified audit events to a SIEM
//   org console DIR PORT             a read-only page on 127.0.0.1 for owners and administrators
//   org console-key DIR CODE         PIN; approves a passkey waiting at the relay's console
//   org changes DIR                  the changes queued at the relay's console
//   org approve DIR ID               PIN; makes a queued change, signed here
//   org attest DIR [CHAIN,...] [CRL,...]   PIN; a TPM device's platform attestation, in two steps (SPEC 29.5)
//   org audit DIR                    "TIME LOG SEQ ACTION OBJECT DETAIL-HEX" per verified event
//
// Group folders are then used like any shared folder: `device vault ...
// --share ID`, and they appear in `device share list`.

